   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What is known goes first",
     "texto": [
      "If you ask «Who called?», the answer highlights the subject: **Мой брат позвонил** («My brother called»). If you ask «What did your brother do?», the answer highlights the action: **Брат позвонил** («The brother called»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Emphasis",
     "texto": [
      "Russian word order is flexible and helps to mark topic and focus, but there is no fixed rule that «the most important goes last»: context and intonation also matter.",
      "Compare **Я купил книгу вчера** (yesterday I bought a book; the focus may be the time) with **Книгу я купил вчера** (it was the book that I bought yesterday; the object is highlighted or contrasted)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
